{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he smelled the smell of his garments.</b> For he was accustomed to smell." "<b>And he said, See, the smell of my son.</b> Once he smelled the smell of the garments, he said: there is no doubt here. And one must emend the verse to read: see, my son — the smell of these is as the smell of the field. Another interpretation: <b>see, smell</b> — the verb ראה applies to several things, even in the foreign tongue, for example: 'See, I have given the land before you.'" "<b>As the smell of the field.</b> Garments that one wears out to the field — their smell is <b>as the smell of the field</b>, for in them a person goes out to the field." "<b>Which HaShem has blessed.</b> One may say it refers back to <b>my son</b>, whom the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the Land of Israel, as it is written: 'To you and to your seed.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {3 "ה׳ resolved as HaShem per voice rules; א״‎י expanded as the Land of Israel based on the cited verse about the land."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:18.877681629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}